# Multi-Member

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Household
> Next Feature: Reports

---

# Overview

Multi-Member allows multiple users to share and manage finances together within a single Household in Kin Finance.

A Household can have one Owner and multiple Members. Members can view and manage transactions and budgets together, while the Owner controls Accounts and Categories.

In MVP, joining is done via invite code. Email-based invitations are planned for the future.

---

# Goals

- Allow multiple users to share a Household.
- Enable collaborative financial management.
- Maintain clear permission boundaries between Owner and Member.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Owner generates an invite code.
- Member joins a Household using an invite code.
- Owner can remove Members.
- Member list is visible to all Household members.

## Out of Scope

- Email-based invitations (future).
- Multiple Households per user (future).
- Household switching (future).
- Transfer ownership (future).
- Role beyond Owner/Member (future).

---

# User Stories

### Generate Invite Code

As an Owner,

I want to generate an invite code for my Household,

So that I can share it with family members.

---

### Join Household

As a new user,

I want to join an existing Household using an invite code,

So that I can manage finances with my family.

---

### View Members

As a user (Owner or Member),

I want to see who is in my Household,

So that I know who has access to our financial data.

---

### Remove Member

As an Owner,

I want to remove a Member from my Household,

So that I can control who has access.

