# Functional Requirements

## Generate Invite Code

Owner can generate an invite code for their Household.

After success:

- A cryptographically random code is generated (8 alphanumeric characters).
- Code is hashed (HMAC-SHA-256 keyed with a server secret) and stored server-side — plaintext is never persisted.
- Expiry is set to 7 days from creation.
- Max uses is set to 1 (single-use).
- Code is displayed on screen (plaintext, shown once).
- Owner can copy or share the code.

---

## Join Household

User can join a Household by entering a valid invite code.

Server performs atomic redemption:

1. Require a signed-in identity.
2. Atomically check the user has no existing membership (by `userId`); reject with "You are already a member of a Household." if they do.
3. Hash the input code (case-normalized).
4. Look up invitation by `codeHash`.
5. Validate: not expired, not revoked, `useCount < maxUses`.
6. Insert `householdMembership` with role "member".
7. Increment `useCount`.

After success:

- User is added as a Member to the Household.
- User gains access to all Household data (respecting visibility rules).
- User is redirected to the Home Screen.

Failure cases (user-friendly messages):

- "Invalid invite code." — code not found.
- "This invite code has expired." — past expiry date.
- "This invite code has already been used." — useCount >= maxUses.
- "This invite code has been revoked." — owner revoked it.

---

## View Members

The application retrieves the list of Members in the current Household.

- Each Member shows: name, email, role badge (Owner/Member).
- Owner sees all Members.
- Member sees all Members.

---

## Remove Member

Owner can remove a Member from the Household.

After success:

- Member is removed.
- Member loses access to Household data immediately.
- Member's Transactions and Budgets remain in the system.

---

# Validation

## Invite Code

- Required.
- Format: 8 alphanumeric characters (no prefix needed).
- Case-normalized before hashing.
- Server-side rate limiting: max 5 redemption attempts per code per minute (per-code bucket), in addition to redemption limits across actors (userId), IPs, and devices.

---

# Empty State

## No Other Members

Title

> You're the only member

Description

> Invite family members to manage finances together.

Primary Action

> Invite Member

---

# Error State

Show messages that are easy to understand.

Examples:

- Invalid invite code.
- Invite code has expired.
- You are already a member of a Household.
- Failed to remove member.
- Please try again.

Do not show technical backend errors.

---

# Success Criteria

Feature is considered complete when:

- Owner can generate an invite code.
- Member can join a Household using an invite code.
- Member is added as "member" role.
- Owner can remove a Member.
- Member list is visible to all.
- Owner cannot be removed.
- Validation works correctly.
- Empty State is available.
- Error State is available.

